From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:29:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: show polls and vote on them from the app

* Show a poll as a poll

A poll is rendered as a "poll:<base64 JSON>" token (question, options,
how many may be chosen) instead of a numbered text list, so the app can
draw the options. The option hashes are still filled in for matching
votes.

* Vote on polls from the app

Votes from the app arrive through "webos-im-send-poll-vote" (account,
chat, poll id, the full selection separated by 0x1f) and are sent with
BuildPollVote(). That needs the poll's original chat and sender exactly
as whatsmeow stored its message secret, which the message cache keeps
for the ?vote command. This is a separate function from ?vote's
send_poll_vote, as the app names the poll by id and its options by name.

When the poll is no longer cached, or was cached before the source was
kept, the sender the transport stashes as
"webos-pollvote-sender" is used, trying both its phone-number and LID
forms against the message secret store.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
